IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pta-small-estates`

-- Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA), ss 2, 7-12, 14, 18, 38A-38B, 45, 47A, 62 Public Trustee Regulations 1942 reg 10A and Trustee Companies Regulations 1988 reg 4, a small estate and the Public Trustee -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_wa_public-trustee-act-1941_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Life facts are from the workbench scenario au/wa/cradle-to-grave-jake/facts.json, event k098 (2 May 2079): Jake dies at
-- 72, divorced, with no will, leaving "an estate of $38,000 and the apartment"; Ruby, 46, his only child, takes all
-- (Administration Act 1903 s 14, item 5). The scenario gives no value for the apartment; $600,000 is the encoder's, as in
-- the Administration Act 1903 baseline, so the gross value used is $638,000. That Ruby lives in WA and is willing and
-- able to administer is ASSUMED, as that baseline assumed. The s 14 prescribed amount is $50 000 (Trustee Companies
-- Regulations 1988 reg 4, unamended since 1988), so with the apartment Jake's estate is too large for a s 14 election and
-- the $38,000 alone would not be.
-- Variants change one fact each. Fees are the encoder's figures, chosen for arithmetic; no scale is deposited.

